  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Brands and agencies pay for messages that move people and for honest measurement. They judge you by portfolio, numbers and client trust.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing a clear message for one audience.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and MBA in communication media and advertising: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft copy and suggest ideas. Routine copy shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Strategy, audience judgment and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and edit; later, own brand decisions.
  </p>

